# Vulnerabilities deliberately not blocking CI. Every entry needs a reason and a date;
# an ignore file without them becomes a place where findings go to be forgotten.
#
# Scope note: this suppresses the *gate*, not the report. Trivy still prints these.

# CVE-2026-34070 — HIGH — langchain-core 0.3.86, path traversal in the legacy
# langchain_core.prompts.loading helpers (load_prompt and friends read file paths out of
# a deserialized config dict without validating traversal or absolute paths).
#
# Not reachable here. This project has no call to load_prompt, load_chain, or anything in
# prompts.loading — verified by grep across every .py file. Prompts are string constants
# in app/prompts.py and are never deserialized from user input or from disk. The
# vulnerability needs an application that loads prompt configs from an untrusted source.
#
# The fix is langchain-core 1.2.22, i.e. the 0.3 -> 1.x major upgrade across langchain,
# langchain-community, langchain-chroma, langchain-ollama, langchain-huggingface,
# langchain-anthropic and langchain-text-splitters. That is a migration, not a version
# bump, and doing it under a CI gate for an unreachable finding is how a security control
# gets disabled rather than satisfied.
#
# Revisit: with the langchain 1.x migration, or immediately if this project ever calls
# load_prompt. Added 2026-08-16.
CVE-2026-34070
